 private:
+    // Called from canPresent() while occluded, instead of attempting a real present. Uses
+    // DXGI_PRESENT_TEST, which runs the occlusion check without presenting any data --
+    // Microsoft's documented recovery pattern for DXGI_STATUS_OCCLUDED (DXGI programming guide,
+    // "Care and feeding of the swap chain"). Unlike a real Present1, this can't consume or
+    // depend on a frame-latency wait slot, since nothing is actually submitted that would need
+    // to retire -- safe to call on every readiness check for as long as we're in standby.
+    //
+    // Distinguishes a genuine failure from "still occluded" (added 2026-10-11, after review
+    // caught that the original version of this method could not tell them apart): a true
+    // FAILED(hr) here -- e.g. DXGI_ERROR_DEVICE_REMOVED -- is not occlusion, and polling forever
+    // against something that can never return S_OK would hang the editor instead of just
+    // flickering. On a genuine failure, exit standby (so the *next* real Present1 attempt in
+    // paint() runs, and its own existing FAILED(hr) handling deals with it properly) rather than
+    // staying latched in this loop. Only a non-S_OK *success* code (still occluded) keeps
+    // polling.
+    bool pollForRecovery()
+    {
+        DXGI_PRESENT_PARAMETERS testParams{};
+        const auto hr = chain->Present1 (0, DXGI_PRESENT_TEST, &testParams);
+
+        if (hr == S_OK)
+        {
+            // Confirmed recovered. Let the very next real frame through immediately rather than
+            // demanding a fresh wait first -- nothing (real or otherwise) has actually been
+            // presented in a while, so there's nothing yet to pace against. Normal throttling
+            // resumes from that next real present onward, via didPresent().
+            occluded = false;
+            didWait = true;
+            return true;
+        }
+
+        if (FAILED (hr))
+        {
+            occluded = false; // not occlusion -- let the next real present's own failure path handle it.
+            return false;
+        }
+
+        return false; // still occluded (some other non-S_OK success code) -- stay in standby.
+    }
